                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers [/h1]\n\nSo I did not buy this game individually. I got it as part of a cheap VR bundle. I was not excited to play this game but it's being listed on the first page of the Steam VR sales list for some reason. I thought I may as well go check it out, especially since it doesn't currently have any negative reviews. Long story short, this game sucks. There's almost no redeeming value. You throw stuff & break stuff. You lay dueces. And you get to shoot a toy gun at a museum. And there's a global leaderboard. Sadly, if you're in the top 5 that just means you are a horrible person.\n\n[h1] Positives [/h1]\n+ it works on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers \n+ the game looks and plays just like the screenshots / video on the store page\n\n[h1] Negatives [/h1]\n- Experienced everything the game had in 10 minutes\n- those are 10 minutes of my life I will never get back\n- writing this review is more fun than the actual game\n- poor graphics\n- wonky throwing mechanics\n- clunky UI\n- using a poor kid as part of the cover art for this game\n\nRate 3/10. It's bad. It's not so bad it's good, it's just bad. I'm just glad I got it as part of a bundle so I didn't waste my money on this game specifically, as this was the worst of the bunch. The others made up for this load of literal crap.\n\np.s. we need a proper fecal throwing game with actual physics & smooth gameplay",
